@doc smysl/0.1 { id: v/multi, granularity: { profile: default } }

@claim c/two { status: speculative }
~ Two separate things went wrong in the eu-west shard last week.

The connection pool saturated under the new concurrency limit introduced by the
4.2 rollout, which pushed acquisition wait from two milliseconds to well over
three hundred.

The credential cache was also evicting far more aggressively than intended after
the same rollout, which added a second independent source of latency on the same
request path.
